WEBVTT

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:14.300
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:22.680
aoku nemuru mizu no hoshi ni sotto

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:22.680
Kissing softly the star of water that sleeps in blue,

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:31.410
kuchizuke shite inochi no hi wo tomosu hito yo

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:31.410
A person who lights the fire of life,

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:36.300
toki to iu kin'iro no sazanami wa

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:36.300
The time, the golden ripple,

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:45.070
oozora no kuchibiru ni umareta toiki ne

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:45.070
is a sigh from the lips of the sky,

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.300
kokoro ni uzumoreta

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.300
The stars of kindness...

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.270
yasashisa no hoshitachi ga

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.270
...buried in heart flame up...

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:56.440
honoo age yobiau

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:56.440
...and call to each other,

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:03.430
namima sasurau nanpasen no you ni

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:03.430
Like wrecked ships wandering on the waves...

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:08.870
mou nakanaide ima

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:08.870
Don't cry, any more,

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:16.240
anata wo sagashite iru hito ga iru kara

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:16.240
because now there is a person looking for you,

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.970
omae ni aitai yo to

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.970
Dying to see you...

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:35.100
The Jupitris Infiltration

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:53.680
You're late.

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:56.620
What's this about enemy vessels
gathering close to Side 2?

00:01:57.260 --> 00:01:58.550
Lieutenant Quattro.

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:00.890
There are numerous rumors
going around...

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:03.760
...since you returned
from Earth alone, Lieutenant.

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:04.960
I'm aware of that.

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:06.690
Is it wise to let them spread?

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:09.460
I intended to talk to you two
sooner or later.

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:11.460
The rumors are true.

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:15.570
Commodore Blex is no longer with us.

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:18.640
But there isn't time to mourn his passing.

00:02:18.710 --> 00:02:22.670
There's an operation we must execute
before heading to Side 2, isn't there?

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:25.850
- Guess that's the reality of war.
- Yeah.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:27.380
I agree.

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:31.120
All right. All right.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:36.260
- Hurry and take off the knee armor as well!
- Okay!

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:38.490
They take forever to do anything!

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:40.560
Is this the one you picked up
by the enemy's ship?

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:43.400
Yeah, and they expect us to
make it operational. They're crazy.

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:44.660
Hey, crane!

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.730
Move it slowly!

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:48.600
Will a model this old actually move?

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:51.610
It only has to <i>look</i> like a Gelgoog.

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:55.880
The insides are almost all recycled from
the Nemos we kept for spare parts.

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:57.970
That's the only way
we can get it to move.

00:02:58.050 --> 00:03:00.420
But what use does it have
other than a dummy guard?

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:02.110
It's not capable of battle, is it?

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:03.820
Huh? Didn't you hear?

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:06.190
- About what?
- From Ensign Reccoa.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:07.280
From Ensign Reccoa?

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:11.120
Ensign Reccoa is using the Gelgoog
to sneak into the Jupitris.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.720
By Jupitris, you mean the one
from Jupiter?

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:14.630
Hey!

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:16.930
I told you, we don't need the rifle!

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:25.440
<i>Miss Reccoa...!</i>

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:27.910
<i>Like she did at Jaburo.</i>

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:34.710
- Kamille!
- Kamille! How are you?!

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:36.520
Fa, have you seen Ensign Reccoa?

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:39.710
The Ensign was going to give
the children who came...

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:41.730
...with Lieutenant Quattro
a tour of the ship.

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:42.760
Thanks.

00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:48.560
I hear Miss Reccoa's
sneaking into the enemy's battleship.

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:50.160
Sneaking in?

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:52.260
She keeps doing things
out of the ordinary.

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:55.500
- Is Miss Reccoa going alone?
- Yeah!

00:03:57.740 --> 00:03:59.340
Here, have some juice.

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:00.670
Thank you.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:01.710
Miss Reccoa.

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:05.010
Is it true that you're sneaking onto
the Jupitris?

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:08.120
Would you care for some?

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:12.120
Miss Reccoa!

00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:13.460
Kamille.

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:15.060
This is a mission.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:17.220
But even at Jaburo, you almost...!

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:19.330
It's too dangerous.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:20.460
You're right.

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:22.400
You certainly saved me that time.

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:24.700
You volunteered, didn't you?

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:27.240
Why not take better care of yourself?!

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:30.040
I thought you were more
grown up than that.

00:04:30.140 --> 00:04:32.580
What do you mean by that, Miss Reccoa?

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:34.810
Never mind. Forget it.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:37.680
I won't forget it!

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:39.550
Stop treating me like a child for a change!

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:44.020
Kamille.

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:45.480
What?!

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:48.190
You're acting like a child
by always picking quarrels.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:51.060
Miss Reccoa's already made her decision.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:52.420
Can't you respect that?

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:54.600
Hey!

00:04:54.670 --> 00:04:57.400
- Hey!
- Stop!

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:00.870
- Even I want to be of some use.
- I understand.

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:04.210
Kamille, I can't imagine you have the time
to be worrying about others.

00:05:13.390 --> 00:05:15.480
- Who is it?
- It's Fa.

00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:21.050
May I come in?

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:22.320
Please, come in.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:29.500
You went to Jaburo, and now the Jupitris?

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:30.540
Yes.

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:34.770
But the last time, I wasn't any help.

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:39.640
Did they find out that you were
an A.E.U.G. crewmember?

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:41.680
Naturally.

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:44.540
The opponents are professionals.
They're not easily tricked.

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:47.450
You're lucky to be alive.

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:51.280
But Jaburo was in the midst of moving.

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:54.590
They were too busy
to pay attention to one spy.

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:57.360
And that's why I made it out alive.

00:05:57.430 --> 00:05:58.590
Is that so.

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:00.460
You think I was a little hard on Kamille?

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:02.790
Not at all.

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:04.800
He tends to overlook the feelings of others.

00:06:04.870 --> 00:06:06.600
He doesn't understand that you're
seeking redemption...

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:07.830
...for your humiliation at Jaburo.

00:06:09.170 --> 00:06:10.640
Thank you, Fa.

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:13.910
But let's not bring that up.

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:16.000
I'll leave the Methuss in your hands.

00:06:16.780 --> 00:06:18.250
Miss Reccoa.

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:20.810
These types of missions suit me the best.

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:22.850
That's why I get selected.

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:32.160
- What do you think?
- About what?

00:06:32.230 --> 00:06:33.600
About Ensign Reccoa.

00:06:33.670 --> 00:06:36.190
I think you're better off
not thinking too much about it.

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:37.200
Why not?

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:40.670
She may have limited experience
as a pilot, but she's really something.

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:43.510
That's not what I'm talking about!

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:45.330
I know that.

00:06:45.410 --> 00:06:48.870
However, you look better with her,
over there, Kamille.

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:50.640
Don't worry about it.

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:53.920
What are you
jumping to conclusions about?!

00:06:53.990 --> 00:06:56.280
Don't take on more
than you can handle at your age.

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:02.180
What are you standing around here for?!

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:05.990
Wh-What are you doing?!

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:09.660
We can talk anyplace!

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:12.500
The Ensign has accepted this
mission to save herself from suffering.

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:14.040
That's why...

00:07:14.110 --> 00:07:15.600
...she could go off
the deep end!

00:07:15.670 --> 00:07:18.230
Losing your temper like that
isn't helping anyone.

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:19.800
That's not true!

00:07:20.780 --> 00:07:21.970
Try to understand!

00:07:22.050 --> 00:07:23.010
I understand!

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:27.480
Trying to help Miss Reccoa now
is just adding salt to her wound.

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:29.490
- I don't get it!
- Stop it!

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:32.580
Fa.

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:34.650
Miss Reccoa is an adult.

00:07:34.730 --> 00:07:38.490
But I can't understand why she acts so
emotionally, like a little girl!

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:40.260
Kamille.

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:41.560
Whatever you say!

00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:43.430
So I'm a little child! Satisfied?!

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:54.340
Do you understand the meaning
of this upcoming operation?

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:56.510
I will take over Side 2 so that...

00:07:57.550 --> 00:08:01.110
...I can obtain a place in the Earth Sphere
where I can walk with you, Sarah.

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:04.250
Do you have a desire for land,
Mr. Paptimus?

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:08.090
No matter how well I'm adapted
to Jupiter's environment...

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:11.360
...even I am a human,
born of a woman's womb.

00:08:11.930 --> 00:08:14.330
So you're hoping for the revival of Earth.

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:15.590
That's right.

00:08:15.670 --> 00:08:18.030
That's why I want a place
for myself until that time comes.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:19.590
And "that place" is the colony?

00:08:26.910 --> 00:08:29.240
I hope that you can help me, Sarah.

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:31.220
Yes.

00:08:36.590 --> 00:08:38.420
I will return to the Jupitris.

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:40.650
I'll have Sarah standby
on the Dogosse Gier.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:52.100
Ensign Reccoa.

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:53.140
Kamille.

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:57.970
I'll back you up with the Zeta Gundam.

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:01.070
Please. But I will be sneaking in alone.

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:02.110
Right!

00:09:10.390 --> 00:09:14.380
<i>Ensign. Upon your escape from the Jupitris,</i>
<i>head directly for Side 2 airspace.</i>

00:09:15.190 --> 00:09:18.820
<i>At worst, you should be able to make</i>
<i>contact with an A.E.U.G. vessel.</i>

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:20.760
Roger, Captain.

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:22.530
<i>I pray for your success.</i>

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:25.730
<i>We're talking escape</i>
<i>even before I sneak in?</i>

00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:33.770
Reccoa, taking off!

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:45.950
Kamille, let's do it!

00:09:52.830 --> 00:09:55.890
Captain Bright,
why did you send Kamille out?

00:09:56.030 --> 00:09:58.000
Ensign Reccoa should've gone out alone!

00:09:58.070 --> 00:09:59.770
From a strategic point of view...

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:01.810
...launching the Zeta for support
may be unnecessary.

00:10:02.570 --> 00:10:05.200
However, when thinking of
Ensign Reccoa's safety...

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:07.250
...Captain Bright's measures are correct.

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:08.740
They aren't!

00:10:08.810 --> 00:10:10.410
Don't think of it
from a man's perspective!

00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:13.450
This is the military!
Gender is irrelevant!

00:10:13.850 --> 00:10:17.720
She may be a soldier, but Ensign Reccoa
is a woman first and foremost!

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:21.190
Such opinions only count
after peace is achieved!

00:10:24.460 --> 00:10:25.620
Excuse me!

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:27.630
Captain Henken!

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:29.220
Hm? Let's return to the Radish.

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:36.840
What Fa's saying is correct.

00:10:38.610 --> 00:10:40.270
Girls will always be girls.

00:10:46.720 --> 00:10:47.910
Here you are.

00:10:48.590 --> 00:10:51.520
I'll have you sortie for
Ensign Reccoa's backup as well.

00:10:51.620 --> 00:10:52.560
Why's that?!

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:53.990
So you'll act more seriously!

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:55.650
Is that the reason?

00:10:55.730 --> 00:10:56.920
You're very high-handed.

00:10:57.930 --> 00:11:00.420
I'm the one giving out orders. Go!

00:11:01.370 --> 00:11:02.630
Petty Officer Fa Yuiry!

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:04.330
Taking off in the Methuss!

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:38.460
There's no mistake about it.

00:11:39.610 --> 00:11:40.830
It's a mobile suit.

00:11:40.910 --> 00:11:42.370
It's headed for the Jupitris.

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:44.940
And ignoring our fleet?

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:45.940
Captain.

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:47.500
Shall I sortie?

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:49.670
We're unsure whether it's an enemy or ally.

00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:52.050
It may be chasing after Mr. Paptimus.

00:11:54.420 --> 00:11:57.390
What if something should happen to him?

00:11:58.790 --> 00:11:59.650
You may launch.

00:12:33.990 --> 00:12:37.220
The information is correct.
This warship operates independently.

00:12:45.170 --> 00:12:46.800
It's huge.

00:13:10.130 --> 00:13:12.860
I'm amazed that she was riding around
in such an old model.

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:16.060
- How much will you sell it for?
- It doesn't seem to be a replica.

00:13:16.130 --> 00:13:18.860
It's a pretty popular type among collectors.

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:20.910
How much do you think it cost me
to restore it?

00:13:21.040 --> 00:13:22.530
You're free to test-drive it...

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:24.200
...but you should've filled it up
before flying it.

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:27.970
I did the calculations, but its mileage
is much worse than I thought.

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:28.880
Hey!

00:13:29.510 --> 00:13:30.950
I'm done checking it.

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:33.810
This mobile suit is nothing but a toy.

00:13:33.890 --> 00:13:35.110
I'll need to frisk you.

00:13:37.060 --> 00:13:40.320
I have no interest in men
who abuse their authority.

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:42.290
You lose.

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:44.590
I've already done an auto check
on the lady.

00:13:44.660 --> 00:13:47.190
And, you're a Spacenoid
from which colony?

00:13:47.270 --> 00:13:48.600
It's the captain.

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:06.880
So that's Paptimus Scirocco.

00:14:11.390 --> 00:14:12.910
It's been thirty minutes.

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:14.890
I hope everything's okay
with Miss Reccoa.

00:14:15.990 --> 00:14:16.960
What?!

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:19.790
How did it find me?!

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:25.970
Great skills! But something's different.

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:31.230
That's the Zeta Gundam!

00:14:31.940 --> 00:14:35.670
But that mobile armor isn't piloted
by the man in question, is it?

00:14:36.380 --> 00:14:37.710
If you're targeting Mr. Paptimus...!

00:14:41.350 --> 00:14:42.750
This mobile suit has such power!

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:44.020
Mr. Paptimus!

00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:45.680
That voice!

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:46.690
Sarah Zabiarov!

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:47.620
I won't lose!

00:15:09.150 --> 00:15:12.170
<i>They're also developing</i>
<i>new mobile suit models.</i>

00:15:14.290 --> 00:15:17.220
What? From the asteroid belt to Earth?

00:15:17.290 --> 00:15:19.590
Yes, the ones known as the Axis.

00:15:20.030 --> 00:15:22.150
Do they plan to ally
with the Titans?

00:15:22.490 --> 00:15:23.720
Well, I can't be sure.

00:15:23.800 --> 00:15:25.190
Fundamentally...

00:15:25.260 --> 00:15:27.530
...the Titans are no different from Zeon.
Which means...!

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:31.000
Hey! Normal suit! What are you doing?

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:33.660
Y-Yes? Um...!

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:35.140
I... I lost my way.

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:37.870
- You lost your way?
- Y-Yes.

00:15:37.940 --> 00:15:39.810
- Which division do you belong to?
- There she is!

00:15:40.310 --> 00:15:42.870
This woman is the castaway
I reported to you!

00:15:42.950 --> 00:15:44.420
What's she doing here?

00:15:44.480 --> 00:15:46.110
The hand grip malfunctioned, so...!

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:47.520
You're lying!

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:48.680
It's true.

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:52.020
Or perhaps I held the hand grip incorrectly.

00:16:06.710 --> 00:16:07.730
Why'd you...?!

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:10.630
Tell me your name.
And your division.

00:16:19.050 --> 00:16:22.750
Reccoa Londe. I'm from Side 2,
Colony 85...

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:28.150
It's me.

00:16:28.230 --> 00:16:29.190
What?!

00:16:29.360 --> 00:16:32.090
Captain, line of fire seen
15 degrees portside.

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:33.320
An enemy attack?

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:35.460
It appears to be a battle
between mobile suits.

00:16:35.670 --> 00:16:36.830
Reccoa Londe.

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:39.670
I hope your journey is an enjoyable one.

00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:43.240
If you can get back safely, that is.

00:16:48.180 --> 00:16:51.510
<i>That man. Does he know who I am?</i>

00:16:53.720 --> 00:16:54.690
Damn!

00:16:56.660 --> 00:16:58.320
Without your weapon...!

00:17:02.460 --> 00:17:03.830
I've still got my rifle!

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:11.800
I'll defeat you!
For my master!

00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:18.310
An enemy?!

00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:19.980
Kamille.

00:17:20.050 --> 00:17:21.810
Fa?! Why are you here?

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:25.510
I'll use the Grenade Launcher!

00:17:33.290 --> 00:17:34.280
Fa! Take it easy!

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:39.630
It <i>is</i> the Messala.
But I can't identify the enemy.

00:17:40.300 --> 00:17:43.200
I know. It's the Zeta Gundam.

00:17:43.270 --> 00:17:46.170
I can feel it... that pressure.

00:17:46.470 --> 00:17:47.440
Captain.

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:51.770
Two against one. Given Sarah's
abilities, that's too great a burden.

00:17:51.840 --> 00:17:53.610
We'll send out the Palace Athene.

00:17:53.680 --> 00:17:54.650
Yes, sir.

00:17:54.850 --> 00:17:56.640
- Wait.
- Sir?

00:17:59.880 --> 00:18:00.870
Is that right?

00:18:00.950 --> 00:18:03.750
You want to get through this battle alone,
do you, Sarah?

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:07.490
The Jupitris will remain on standby,
at level one battle station.

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:08.530
Yes, sir.

00:18:08.830 --> 00:18:11.730
<i>Sarah... You're so adorable.</i>

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:15.030
Excuse me. Can you see
the mobile suit battle from here?

00:18:15.100 --> 00:18:16.070
Yeah!

00:18:17.270 --> 00:18:20.170
Are you the one who came on board
in that unusual mobile suit?

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:21.830
Oh! I saw a flash!

00:18:21.910 --> 00:18:24.240
- You are hot, lady!
- Thank you!

00:18:24.310 --> 00:18:26.870
We don't have anyone like you
on the Jupitris.

00:18:26.950 --> 00:18:30.540
- How flattering.
- I'm serious! I'm not just saying it.

00:18:32.650 --> 00:18:34.640
Sorry, guess I'm too hot
for you to handle.

00:18:37.160 --> 00:18:39.120
Captain, the hatch on the third deck
is opening.

00:18:39.590 --> 00:18:40.420
What?!

00:18:40.490 --> 00:18:42.190
I haven't given orders for anyone
to take off!

00:18:42.260 --> 00:18:43.750
Controller!

00:18:43.830 --> 00:18:44.890
Answer, controller!

00:18:44.960 --> 00:18:46.930
It's likely Reccoa Londe.

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:49.470
The lady wants to go home.

00:18:50.300 --> 00:18:51.860
What are the guards doing?!

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:53.060
Let her go.

00:18:53.140 --> 00:18:55.660
Don't let yourself be distracted
by some trivial fly.

00:18:55.740 --> 00:18:56.640
But, sir...!

00:18:56.710 --> 00:18:58.300
That woman.

00:18:58.380 --> 00:19:00.210
I could learn to like her.

00:19:06.350 --> 00:19:07.910
Scirocco's ship.

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:12.590
It's too fast.

00:19:15.490 --> 00:19:16.760
She avoided it!

00:19:16.830 --> 00:19:17.850
I can't.

00:19:17.930 --> 00:19:20.590
I'm too disturbed.
If I could keep my cool...!

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:24.570
Another enemy?!

00:19:26.700 --> 00:19:28.430
That mobile armor!

00:19:28.970 --> 00:19:30.910
Ensign Reccoa! Are you all right?!

00:19:31.240 --> 00:19:32.800
Fa! Why are you here?!

00:19:38.250 --> 00:19:39.610
Ensign Reccoa!

00:19:42.090 --> 00:19:43.710
Her power's decreased.

00:19:46.090 --> 00:19:47.080
Impossible.

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:51.960
Not yet!

00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:54.630
Direct hit?!

00:19:55.630 --> 00:19:56.330
From behind!

00:19:58.070 --> 00:19:59.470
Where are you looking?!

00:20:11.350 --> 00:20:13.510
I still can't defeat it.

00:20:14.290 --> 00:20:15.720
She's escaped.

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:18.420
Her timing's good.

00:20:19.790 --> 00:20:22.450
Is she an enemy I can afford to let live?

00:20:25.560 --> 00:20:28.560
I think I lost half the nozzle...
but I'm okay.

00:20:30.270 --> 00:20:33.170
Kamille, Fa, we're getting out of here.
Can you keep up?

00:20:33.240 --> 00:20:35.000
I'll bring the Methuss with me.

00:20:35.070 --> 00:20:36.970
Miss Reccoa, please go ahead.

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:38.010
Roger.

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:43.710
Fa, thanks for coming.
You saved me.

00:20:44.020 --> 00:20:45.950
You also saved me.

00:20:46.020 --> 00:20:48.580
Ride the Zeta.
Watch out for enemies behind us.

00:20:48.650 --> 00:20:49.620
Roger!

00:20:59.060 --> 00:21:00.830
I did my best, but...

00:21:00.900 --> 00:21:02.370
...that mobile suit...

00:21:02.430 --> 00:21:05.800
...I felt strong thoughts,
unlike those I feel from you, Mr. Paptimus.

00:21:05.870 --> 00:21:07.240
Okay. It's all right.

00:21:08.070 --> 00:21:10.370
You've accomplished
more than I hoped for.

00:21:11.180 --> 00:21:13.140
Mr. Paptimus.

00:21:17.050 --> 00:21:18.680
Get some sleep, Sarah.

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:21.740
I'll need you to help me
with my next plan.

00:21:22.320 --> 00:21:23.290
Y-Yes.

00:21:28.290 --> 00:21:29.590
I see.

00:21:29.660 --> 00:21:32.150
Your observation skills are amazing,
Ensign Reccoa.

00:21:32.230 --> 00:21:32.990
Thank you.

00:21:33.060 --> 00:21:35.760
- What's this?
- Oh, that?

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:38.470
I was desperate in my escape...

00:21:38.540 --> 00:21:40.060
...so I can't be sure about that.

00:21:40.840 --> 00:21:42.070
Is that so?

00:21:44.040 --> 00:21:46.010
Can I see that, please?

00:21:59.460 --> 00:22:01.430
I-I can't remember.

00:22:02.360 --> 00:22:04.490
Ensign Reccoa, get some rest.

00:22:04.560 --> 00:22:06.290
I'm sorry about that.

00:22:06.360 --> 00:22:09.230
Well, it's not the type of mission
you're accustomed to.

00:22:09.300 --> 00:22:10.270
Later.

00:22:15.970 --> 00:22:20.100
"Why didn't I tell Bright
about Paptimus Scirocco?"

00:22:20.480 --> 00:22:22.910
Right now, Reccoa does not have an answer.

00:22:23.950 --> 00:22:28.250
And this unanswered question will
remain a sore spot in Reccoa's heart.

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:46.470 --> 00:23:50.370
The Alexandria commences a gas attack
on a Side 2 Colony.

00:23:51.410 --> 00:23:54.640
Several million lives in the colony
are in danger.

00:23:54.750 --> 00:23:57.610
Emma dashes toward
the attached gas cylinder.

00:23:58.080 --> 00:24:01.520
In the meantime, adults are engaged
in dark struggles behind the scenes.

00:24:02.290 --> 00:24:07.020
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"Crisis at Side 2".

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:12.440
Next Episode

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:12.440
Crisis at Side 2

00:24:07.520 --> 00:24:10.390
You will see the tears of time.
